{#-
  Source-grounding audit pack (WeasyPrint).

  Structure mirrors audit_pack_pdf.py exactly:
    - Institution band (institution name + study title + rule).
    - Title "Source-Grounding Audit Pack" + eyebrow "Expert source-audit worksheet".
    - Instructions paragraph + the 0/1/2 scale legend.
    - One card per audit item: "Audit item N · condition · cited ref" head, the
      audit_item_id, lesson objective, generated excerpt (markdown), cited source
      (id) + snippet, topic/scope boundary, then a 4-criteria table (Source
      relevance / Support sufficiency / Faithfulness / Scope correctness) each with
      0/1/2 single-select circle markers + a Comment column.

  All dynamic text passes through Jinja autoescaping; the generated excerpt is the
  one trusted exception — it is escaped first, then rendered as markdown by
  renderer._render_markdown, and emitted with the `safe` filter.
-#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Source-Grounding Audit Pack</title>
  <style>{{ stylesheet | safe }}</style>
</head>
<body>
  {#- Hoist the pack code into a named string for the per-page footer. -#}
  <div class="packet-code-anchor">{{ pack_code }}</div>

  <p class="institution">{{ institution_name }}</p>
  <p class="study-title">{{ study_title }}</p>
  <hr class="band-rule">

  <h1 class="doc-title">Source-Grounding Audit Pack</h1>
  <p class="eyebrow">Expert source-audit worksheet</p>

  <p class="body">
    For each item below, judge whether the cited source from
    <strong>{{ textbook_name }}</strong> supports the generated excerpt. Score every
    criterion <strong>0</strong> (fail), <strong>1</strong> (partial/unclear), or
    <strong>2</strong> (pass). This is a separate check from the reading-note
    quality rating.
  </p>
  <p class="legend">
    0 = criterion not met &#183; 1 = some support, incomplete/ambiguous &#183; 2 = clearly met
  </p>

  {% if not items %}
  <p class="body">No audit items have been built for this experiment yet.</p>
  {% endif %}

  {% for item in items %}
  <section class="audit-item">
    <p class="item-head">Audit item {{ item.index }}</p>
    <p class="meta">{{ item.audit_id }}</p>
    <hr class="item-rule">

    <p class="label">Lesson objective</p>
    <p class="body">{{ item.objective }}</p>

    <div class="audit-compare">
      <div class="audit-compare-cell">
        <p class="label">Generated excerpt</p>
        <div class="markdown">{{ item.excerpt_html | safe }}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="audit-compare-cell">
        <p class="label">Cited source ({{ item.source_id }})</p>
        <div class="source markdown">{{ item.snippet_html | safe }}</div>
        {#- Render the cited figure beside the snippet when the source record
            is a VisualBlock. ``figure_url`` is the renderer-resolved src (local
            cache when available, original URL otherwise); ``figure_caption``
            may be empty. Both fields are None for text-only sources, in which
            case nothing renders — no broken <img>. -#}
        {% if item.figure_url %}
        <figure class="audit-figure">
          <img src="{{ item.figure_url }}" alt="{{ item.figure_caption or 'Cited textbook figure' }}">
          {% if item.figure_caption %}<figcaption>{{ item.figure_caption }}</figcaption>{% endif %}
        </figure>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="meta scope">Topic/scope boundary: {{ item.scope }}</p>

    <table class="criteria-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="crit-head">Criterion</th>
          <th class="score-head">0</th>
          <th class="score-head">1</th>
          <th class="score-head">2</th>
          <th class="comment-head">Comment</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for criterion in criteria %}
        <tr>
          <td class="crit-cell">
            <span class="crit-label">{{ criterion.label }}</span>
            <span class="crit-desc">{{ criterion.description }}</span>
          </td>
          <td class="score-cell"><span class="marker marker-circle"></span></td>
          <td class="score-cell"><span class="marker marker-circle"></span></td>
          <td class="score-cell"><span class="marker marker-circle"></span></td>
          <td class="comment-cell"></td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
</body>
</html>
